<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63969" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοχ-ᾱγός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόχος, ἄγω</span>), 
			Dor.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοχηγός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>leader of an armed band</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				141
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Theophil.
				3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> esp.
				<i>commander of a company</i> (<i><span class="en">
				100
			</span></i> men), <i>captain</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				3.1.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				3p.8
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, etc.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξίαρχος</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			in the Spartan army, <i>commander of a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόχος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.66
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Lac.</u>
				11.4
			</span></i>, etc.; in the Persian army, <i>captain</i> of <i><span class="en">
				24
			</span></i> men, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.3.21
			</span></i>, etc.; = Lat. <i>centurio</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cam.</u>
				37
			</span></i>; also, =
			<i>curio</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.7
			</span></i>.—The word, 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυναγός</span>
			, was always used in the 
				Dor.
			 form by Attic authors.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
